REM Protects a comment at a position where a statement legally begins from a false
REM line-break-check alarm: a comment alone on a ':'-continuation line whose
REM preceding statement line ends in a ';' separator, a comment alone on a
REM ':'-continuation line whose preceding line ends in the word THEN, and a comment
REM directly after THEN on the same physical line. Upper, lower and mixed case.
COUNT=1
IF COUNT=1 THEN IF COUNT=1 THEN LET COUNT=1 ELSE LET COUNT=2 FI;
: REM comment after a separator-ended continuation, upper case
if count=1 then if count=1 then let count=1 else let count=2 fi;
: rem comment after a separator-ended continuation, lower case
If Count=1 Then
:  Rem comment after a THEN-ended continuation, mixed case
IF COUNT=1 THEN
: REM comment after a THEN-ended continuation, single space
if count=1 then rem comment directly after THEN on the same line
